From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] powershell: pass our standard handles to PowerShell 7

run_pwsh() started pwsh with bInheritHandles TRUE but without
STARTF_USESTDHANDLES, so with no console (CREATE_NO_WINDOW) pwsh got no
standard handles: "powershell -Command ..." printed nothing into a pipe or
a file and could not read piped input. Pass ours explicitly.
---
--- a/programs/powershell/main.c
+++ b/programs/powershell/main.c
@@ -99,6 +99,15 @@
      * Wine does not (sg-session: "pwsh needs a console") */
     flags = GetConsoleMode(GetStdHandle(STD_INPUT_HANDLE), &mode)
             || GetConsoleMode(GetStdHandle(STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE), &mode) ? 0 : CREATE_NO_WINDOW;
+    /* pwsh reads and writes what we were given: a pipe or a file when
+     * "powershell -c ... | more" or "> out.txt" -- without these it would get
+     * no standard handles at all once there is no console to share */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PS_NO_STDHANDLES
+    si.dwFlags = STARTF_USESTDHANDLES;
+    si.hStdInput = GetStdHandle(STD_INPUT_HANDLE);
+    si.hStdOutput = GetStdHandle(STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE);
+    si.hStdError = GetStdHandle(STD_ERROR_HANDLE);
+#endif
     if (!CreateProcessW(pwsh, cmd, NULL, NULL, TRUE, flags, NULL, NULL, &si, &pi))
     {
         free(cmd);
